# Headscale (Tailscale control plane) reverse-proxy. Activated when
# Remote Hosts is enabled. Hostname comes from
# SYNAPSE_HEADSCALE_DOMAIN (explicit override) OR falls back to
# headscale.<SYNAPSE_DOMAIN> / headscale.<SYNAPSE_BASE_DOMAIN>.
#
# v1.19.7+: TLS is issued ON-DEMAND, gated by the global
# on_demand_tls { ask } directive (which points at
# /v1/internal/tls_ask). The api approves the headscale host there.
# Why on-demand instead of standard ACME (`tls <email>`): when the
# Caddyfile also carries a `:443 { tls { on_demand } }` catch-all
# (every install with deployments does), Caddy's config adapter
# silently EXCLUDES a more-specific `tls <email>` site from its
# automatic-management list, so the cert never preloads and the
# handshake fails with a TLS alert. Routing on-demand through the
# same ask gate the deployments already use issues the cert lazily
# and reliably. Tailscale client WebSockets need no extra config.
{{SYNAPSE_HEADSCALE_HOST}} {
    tls {
        on_demand
    }
    reverse_proxy synapse-headscale:8080 {
        header_up X-Real-IP {remote_host}
        header_up X-Forwarded-For {remote_host}
        header_up X-Forwarded-Proto {scheme}
        header_up X-Forwarded-Host {host}
    }
}